{"content":[{"c":["RUTH (P",{"c":["erson"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Moabitess and the widow of Mahlon, the son of Naomi and Elimelech, who were Ephrathites from Bethlehem living in Moab because of a severe famine in Judah. After the death of Elimelech and Naomi’s two sons, Naomi returned to Bethlehem with her daughter-in-law Ruth during the time of the barley harvest (",{"href":"?bref=Ruth.1.4-22","r":"Ruth.1.4-22","rawR":"Ruth.1.4-22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ruth.1.4-22","value":"Ruth.1.4-22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ru 1:4-22"},"). While gleaning in the barley fields of Boaz, Ruth found favor in his eyes (",{"href":"?bref=Ruth.2.2-22","r":"Ruth.2.2-22","rawR":"Ruth.2.2-22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ruth.2.2-22","value":"Ruth.2.2-22"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:2-22"},"). She later married Boaz, when he, serving as nearest kin to the childless Naomi, purchased Naomi’s estate to keep it within the family (",{"href":"?bref=Ruth.4.5-13","r":"Ruth.4.5-13","rawR":"Ruth.4.5-13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ruth.4.5-13","value":"Ruth.4.5-13"}],"t":"ref","v":"4:5-13"},"). Ruth is mentioned in Matthew’s genealogy of Christ as the mother of Obed and the great-grandmother of David (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.1.5","r":"Matt.1.5","rawR":"Matt.1.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.1.5","value":"Matt.1.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 1:5"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Genealogy of Jesus Christ"},"; ",{"href":"?item=RuthBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"RuthBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"RuthBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Ruth, Book of"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"RuthPerson","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ru 1:4-22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ruth.1.4-22","rawQueryValue":"Ruth.1.4-22","sourceRefExact":"Ruth.1.4-22"},{"anchorText":"2:2-22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ruth.2.2-22","rawQueryValue":"Ruth.2.2-22","sourceRefExact":"Ruth.2.2-22"},{"anchorText":"4:5-13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ruth.4.5-13","rawQueryValue":"Ruth.4.5-13","sourceRefExact":"Ruth.4.5-13"},{"anchorText":"Mt 1:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.1.5","rawQueryValue":"Matt.1.5","sourceRefExact":"Matt.1.5"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"5300df945f1340b2eeb8109d1983a3c0e4b85cdb9669e89b4b4fb1781c182bcc","sourceItemName":"RuthPerson","sourceItemOrder":187,"sourceMember":"Articles/R.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"RuthPerson","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Ruth (Person)","title":"Ruth (Person)","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}